{title: 104 - My Shepherd Will Supply My Need}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: God the Father}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C]My Shepherd will supply [G]my [C]need,
[C]Jehovah [Am]is His [Em]name.
[Em]In pastures [Am]fresh He makes [G]me feed
[C]Beside [Am]the living stream.
[Am]He brings my [Em]wand'ring spirit [Am]back
[C]When [Am]I forsake His ways,
[Dm]And leads [C]me, for His [Am]mercy's sake,
[Am]In paths [Bdim]of truth [Am]and grace.

Verse 2:
[C]When I walk through the shades [G]of [C]death,
[C]Thy presence [Am]is my [Em]stay;
[Em]A [G]word [Am]of Thy supporting [G]breath
[C]Drives [G/B]all [Am]my fears away.
[Am]Thy hand in [Em]sight [Am/E]of [Em]all [G]my [Am]foes
[C]Doth [Am]still my table spread;
[Dm]My cup [C]with blessings [Am]over flows,
[Am]Thine oil [Bdim]anoints [Am]my head.

Verse 3:
[C]The sure provisions of [G]my [C]God
[C]Attend me [Am]all my [Em]days;
[Em]O [G]may [Am]Thy house be [G/B]mine abode
[C]And [G/B]all [Am]my work be praise.
[Am]There would [Em]I [Am/E]find [Em]a [G]settled [Am]rest
[C]While [Am]others go and [G]come;
[Dm]No more [C]a stranger [Am]or a guest,
[Am]But like [Bdim]a child [Am]at home.
